From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:31:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(client): routing rules pass the reject method and resolve
 options

Since "feat(client): add route action support" (2025-08-22) the form of a
routing rule offers a method for the reject action (drop packets, don't
drop) and a DNS server, strategy, cache, TTL and client subnet for the
resolve action, but generate_client.uc never put them in the rule: a rule
set to drop packets answered with TCP RST / ICMP port unreachable, and a
resolve rule always went through DNS routing with its defaults.

They are passed now, each only with its own action (sing-box refuses a
field of another action, and a value left over from an earlier action
must not reach the rule). The default reject method writes nothing, so a
configuration without these options is generated as before.

Checked with sing-box 1.12.22, 1.13.11 and 1.14.4 ("sing-box check"): a
drop rule, a reject rule with no_drop, a resolve rule with all five
options and a route rule with leftover reject and resolve values; on a
real configuration only "method": "drop" of its drop rule is added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011cyCFAA9hPeqN8wsgkxbrJ

diff --git a/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc b/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
index a75fe68..ef5be18 100755
--- a/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
+++ b/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
@@ -1147,6 +1147,12 @@ if (!isEmpty(main_node)) {
 		if (ruleset_left_none(rule_set, 'Routing rule', cfg))
 			return null;
 
+		/* The form has a method for reject and a DNS server, strategy, cache,
+		 * TTL and client subnet for resolve; sing-box takes each of them only
+		 * with its own action. */
+		const reject = (cfg.action === 'reject'),
+		      resolve = (cfg.action === 'resolve');
+
 		push(config.route.rules, {
 			ip_version: strToInt(cfg.ip_version),
 			protocol: cfg.protocol,
@@ -1179,7 +1185,14 @@ if (!isEmpty(main_node)) {
 			udp_timeout: strToTime(cfg.udp_timeout),
 			tls_fragment: strToBool(cfg.tls_fragment),
 			tls_fragment_fallback_delay: strToTime(cfg.tls_fragment_fallback_delay),
-			tls_record_fragment: strToBool(cfg.tls_record_fragment)
+			tls_record_fragment: strToBool(cfg.tls_record_fragment),
+			method: (reject && cfg.reject_method === 'drop') ? 'drop' : null,
+			no_drop: reject ? strToBool(cfg.reject_no_drop) : null,
+			server: resolve ? get_resolver(cfg.resolve_server) : null,
+			strategy: resolve ? cfg.resolve_strategy : null,
+			disable_cache: resolve ? strToBool(cfg.resolve_disable_cache) : null,
+			rewrite_ttl: resolve ? strToInt(cfg.resolve_rewrite_ttl) : null,
+			client_subnet: resolve ? cfg.resolve_client_subnet : null
 		});
 	});
 
